& [CheckpointForm] is the complete scheduler frontier
  + [RCC-001] CoordinationCheckpoint is a strict versioned JSON and JsonSchema-capable form
  + [RCC-002] it binds invocation procedure procedure digest IR IR digest admission disposition and digest catalogue generation request digest initial session digest slice index and optional predecessor checkpoint digest
  + [RCC-003] it retains process states steps continuations active continuation references messages delivered references pending reactivations terminal returns trace events logical clock and the initial negotiation session
  + [RCC-004] checkpoint_digest is canonical SHA-256 over the complete form with only checkpoint_digest cleared
  + [RCC-005] it contains no native stack pointer thread future closure host handle ambient cache or hidden neural state

& [StartAndAdvance] are closed pure transitions
  + [RCC-006] BEGIN runs the existing invocation and coordination validation gates before constructing state
  + [RCC-007] BEGIN initializes byte-equal process state session clock and InvocationStarted trace material to the uninterrupted coordinator
  + [RCC-008] ADVANCE requires maximum_steps greater than zero
  + [RCC-009] ADVANCE validates the checkpoint and exact current catalogue procedure IR admission request and initial session bindings before any step
  + [RCC-010] ADVANCE executes at most maximum_steps new process or scheduler steps under the existing deterministic scheduler
  + [RCC-011] caller slice exhaustion returns Paused with exactly one successor checkpoint and no terminal outcome
  + [RCC-012] returned faulted or budget-refused completion returns exactly one existing CoordinationOutcome and no checkpoint
  + [RCC-013] global step trace logical-time message memory and static IR bounds retain their existing terminal fault meanings and take precedence over pause

& [Validation] rejects false reentry
  + [RCC-014] checkpoint validation recomputes its digest exact input lineage and slice-predecessor shape
  + [RCC-015] process map keys definitions invocation references state identities regions instruction indices and remaining budgets must be coherent
  + [RCC-016] continuation map keys digests procedure refs active references and current states must be coherent
  + [RCC-017] message keys session process frame and frontier references plus delivered subsets must be coherent
  + [RCC-018] trace logical indexes procedure refs and causal predecessor chain plus unique step and event identities must be coherent
  + [RCC-019] terminal-return maps pending-reactivation sets logical clock and session lineage must be coherent with retained states
  + [RCC-020] any stale changed corrupt cross-invocation or structurally invalid checkpoint refuses with no successor runtime value

& [Compatibility] has one interpreter
  + [RCC-021] coordinate_catalogued_procedure keeps its public signature and existing invalid-input typed outcome
  + [RCC-022] uninterrupted coordination delegates to the same initialization and drive machinery used by slices
  + [RCC-023] any finite positive quota partition that reaches termination yields a byte-equal terminal outcome for equal exact inputs
  + [RCC-024] repeated equal BEGIN or ADVANCE from equal immutable inputs is byte-equal
  + [RCC-025] inputs and predecessor checkpoints are never mutated and no external effect occurs

& [Boundary] is execution-frame reentry not a new language
  + [RCC-026] ProcessInstanceState remains the P0 frame with instruction cursor typed local state lifecycle wait state message frontier logical time and budgets
  + [RCC-027] SerializedContinuation remains the P0 yielded-process continuation and no native stack capture is introduced
  + [RCC-028] logical call-stack subroutine call return recursion parser or source-syntax changes are deferred
  + [RCC-029] MCP host attention-ledger persistence provider llama.cpp and IDE integration are deferred
  + [RCC-030] digest equality proves internal content binding and determinism not producer authentication semantic truth or neural-state continuation

& [Acceptance] is measurable
  + [RCC-A01] source SJS signature and seven-fold trace verify
  + [RCC-A02] genesis checkpoint validates and equal replay is byte-identical
  + [RCC-A03] quota-one advance pauses with exactly one step and resumes to terminal
  + [RCC-A04] multiple quota partitions equal the uninterrupted outcome byte for byte
  + [RCC-A05] tamper stale cross-input structural and zero-quota cases refuse without successor
  + [RCC-A06] original coordination suite formatting warnings-denied lint full workspace regression manifest audit and scoped Git review pass

